in Ohio, Pennsylvania, Virginia, Kentucky, and Maryland. It also generates, transmits, and distributes electricity to approximately 0.5 million customers in various counties in the northern part of Indiana, as well as engages in wholesale electric and transmission transactions. It owns and operates steam coal generating stations in Wheatfield and Michigan City; combined cycle gas turbine in West Terre Haute; natural gas generating units in Wheatfield; hydro generating plants in Carroll County and White County; wind generating units in White County; and solar generating units in Sullivan County, Gibson County, Jasper County, and White County. The company was formerly known as NIPSCO Industries, Inc. and changed its name to NiSource Inc. in April 1999. NiSource Inc. was founded in 1847 and is headquartered in Merrillville, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lloyd M. Yates | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $866K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["NiSource Inc is a large-cap utilities business with a $21.2B market cap on $6.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 68% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $420M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 62% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6150974767819982},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Gross margin tops the Utilities peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"